# LibreWolf build-fixes.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M2-02 ("Build the common patch set on Android")
#
# This file collects the changes that are needed to make an Android build of the
# LibreWolf tree compile *and that are not attributable to any single LibreWolf
# patch*. Each entry below states the failure it fixes, verbatim, and the
# evidence that the failure is real rather than assumed.
#
# The rule this file exists to serve (docs/android/AGENTS.md, "What not to do"):
# a build error is never fixed by dropping a patch from assets/patches/common.txt.
# Nothing has been dropped, amended or reordered to produce a green build; the
# full 24-entry common list and all three pre-existing android.txt entries are
# applied unchanged, and this file is the ONLY change LW-M2-02 made to any patch
# or patch list.
#
# It contains exactly one hunk. That is the finding, not a placeholder: with the
# straddler splits from M1 in place, the LibreWolf common patch set compiles on
# aarch64-linux-android with no C++, Rust, moz.build or moz.configure change of
# any kind. The single failure is in Gradle, and it is caused by an out-of-patch
# tree mutation (landmine L4), not by any patch.
#
# Applied last in assets/patches/android.txt. It has no ordering constraint with
# anything else: no other patch in common.txt, android.txt or desktop.txt touches
# any file below. Checked with
#     grep -rn '^\(+++ b\|--- a\)/.*build\.gradle' patches/
# which matches this file and nothing else.
#
# THE BUILD THIS FILE MAKES GREEN
#
#   tree      librewolf-153.0esr-1, produced by
#             `python3 scripts/librewolf-patches.py 153.0esr 1 --targets=android`
#             on a freshly extracted, GPG-verified firefox-153.0esr.source.tar.xz
#             (the base ./version.android pins). 24 common + 4 android patches,
#             patcher exit 0, no .rej, 13 hunks with fuzz across 11 patches.
#   mozconfig assets/mozconfig.android, byte for byte, no edit
#   image     librewolf-android-build (LW-M0-06 + LW-M0-15)
#   result    ./mach build -j14  ->  MACH_EXIT=0, 15 min 49 s
#             dist/bin/libxul.so: ELF 64-bit LSB, ARM aarch64, for Android 26,
#                                 built by NDK r29
#             geckoview-debug.aar: 91 MB
#
#   Cross-checked on the release-track base too (librewolf-153.0.4-1, same
#   patch set, same mozconfig): ./mach build exit 0 with this hunk, exit 2
#   without it.
#
#   Everything assets/mozconfig.android asks for survived: MOZ_HARDENING_CFLAGS,
#   MOZ_HARDENING_LDFLAGS, MOZ_STL_HARDENING_FLAGS (_EXTENSIVE), MOZ_MEMORY,
#   MOZ_REPLACE_MALLOC{,_STATIC} and MOZ_RUST_SIMD in the ESR objdir's
#   config.status are identical to LW-M2-01's stock baseline. No hardening
#   option had to be dropped, softened or worked around.
#
#
# ===========================================================================
# 1. build.gradle - computeVersionCode() cannot parse the LibreWolf version
# ===========================================================================
#
# THE FAILURE, verbatim, from ./mach build on librewolf-153.0.4-1 (the full
# common+android patch set, assets/mozconfig.android unmodified, inside the
# pinned librewolf-android-build image):
#
#     3:14.19 W FAILURE: Build failed with an exception.
#     3:14.19 W * Where:
#     3:14.19 W Build file '/work/repo/librewolf-153.0.4-1/build.gradle' line: 199
#     3:14.19 W * What went wrong:
#     3:14.19 W A problem occurred evaluating root project 'librewolf-153.0.4-1'.
#     3:14.19 W > For input string: "4-1"
#     ...
#     3:14.61 E gmake[3]: *** [backend.mk:2401: widget/android/.deps/generated_geckoview_files.stub] Error 1
#     3:14.61 E gmake[2]: *** [config/recurse.mk:34: export] Error 2
#     3:14.61 E gmake[1]: *** [config/rules.mk:357: default] Error 2
#     3:14.61 E gmake: *** [client.mk:58: build] Error 2
#     MACH_EXIT=2
#
# This is a HARD STOP and an early one. It happens in the `export` tier, inside
# `mach android export` (mobile/android/gradle.py:48), while Gradle is still
# evaluating the root project - three minutes in, before a single line of Gecko
# has been compiled. Nothing downstream of it had been proven green when it was
# hit; the green build came afterwards, with this hunk applied.
#
# Every Android build of a LibreWolf tree fails here, on BOTH release and ESR
# tracks, for the same reason and in the same place. The ESR half is not a
# deduction - it was reproduced on the tree ./version.android actually pins, by
# reverting this hunk on an otherwise green librewolf-153.0esr-1 and re-running
# the Gradle half:
#
#     $ patch -p1 -R -i ../patches/android/build-fixes.patch
#     $ ./mach android archive-geckoview
#     FAILURE: Build failed with an exception.
#     * Where:
#     Build file '/work/repo/librewolf-153.0esr-1/build.gradle' line: 195
#     * What went wrong:
#     A problem occurred evaluating root project 'librewolf-153.0esr-1'.
#     > For input string: "0esr-1"
#     BUILD FAILED in 1s
#     MACH_EXIT=1
#
# The two tracks report different line numbers because they die on different
# calls, not because the file differs - build.gradle is line-for-line identical
# in both tarballs here:
#     :195  code += Integer.parseInt(parts[1]) * 100   <- ESR,     parts[1]="0esr-1"
#     :199  code += Integer.parseInt(parts[2])         <- release, parts[2]="4-1"
# Re-applying the hunk restores the file byte for byte and `./mach build` is
# green again.
#
# WHY IT HAPPENS
#
#   * scripts/librewolf-patches.py rewrites browser/config/version.txt and
#     browser/config/version_display.txt to "<version>-<release>" for every
#     target, unconditionally, where <version> is the contents of ./version
#     (desktop) or ./version.android (Android). That write is not expressed as a
#     patch - it is one of the out-of-patch mutations listed under landmine L4 in
#     docs/android/AGENTS.md - so no patch checker sees it.
#
#   * build/moz.configure/init.configure:1063-1153 (`milestone`) resolves
#     MOZ_APP_VERSION from `<build_project>/config/version.txt` *if that file
#     exists*, otherwise from browser/config/version.txt. mobile/android/config/
#     contains only js_wrapper.sh, mozconfigs/ and tooltool-manifests/ - no
#     version.txt - so the loop at :1077-1081 breaks on its first iteration and
#     Android falls back to the browser/ value, i.e. the rewritten one.
#     Confirmed in both object directories:
#         release track  'MOZ_APP_VERSION': '153.0.4-1'   'MOZ_APP_VERSION_DISPLAY': '153.0.4-1'
#         ESR track      'MOZ_APP_VERSION': '153.0esr-1'  'MOZ_APP_VERSION_DISPLAY': '153.0esr-1'
#     Desktop is unaffected because nothing on desktop parses that string into
#     integers.
#
#   * build.gradle:171-172 `getAppVersionWithoutMilestone()` strips only an
#     `[ab][0-9]` nightly/beta milestone, and build.gradle:183-203
#     `computeVersionCode()` then does
#         String[] parts = appVersion.split('\\.')
#         assert parts.size() == 2 || parts.size() == 3
#         int code = Integer.parseInt(parts[0]) * 100000
#         code += Integer.parseInt(parts[1]) * 100
#         if (parts.size() == 3) code += Integer.parseInt(parts[2])
#     "153.0.4-1" splits to ["153", "0", "4-1"] and Integer.parseInt("4-1")
#     throws NumberFormatException. "153.0esr-1" splits to ["153", "0esr-1"],
#     passes the assert, and throws on Integer.parseInt("0esr-1") instead.
#
#     Run against java.lang.String directly (both helpers are plain
#     String.replaceFirst, so the semantics are Java's, not Groovy's):
#         MOZ_APP_VERSION=153.0.4-1   upstream -> "153.0.4-1"  NumberFormatException: For input string: "4-1"
#         MOZ_APP_VERSION=153.0.4-1   patched  -> "153.0.4"    versionCode=15300004
#         MOZ_APP_VERSION=153.0esr-1  upstream -> "153.0esr-1" NumberFormatException: For input string: "0esr-1"
#         MOZ_APP_VERSION=153.0esr-1  patched  -> "153.0"      versionCode=15300000
#         MOZ_APP_VERSION=153.0a1     upstream -> "153.0"      versionCode=15300000   (unchanged by this hunk)
#         MOZ_APP_VERSION=153.0.4     upstream -> "153.0.4"    versionCode=15300004   (unchanged by this hunk)
#
# WHY THE `esr$` STRIP IS HERE, AND WHAT IT REALLY POINTS AT
#
#   Upstream does not hit the ESR half of this. A stock firefox-153.0esr tarball
#   carries
#         browser/config/version.txt          153.0
#         browser/config/version_display.txt  153.0esr
#   so upstream's MOZ_APP_VERSION on the ESR branch is "153.0" and
#   computeVersionCode() is happy. The string "esr" only ever lives in
#   version_display.txt, which build.gradle never reads.
#
#   LibreWolf writes ./version.android ("153.0esr" - the *tarball/track* name,
#   not Firefox's own version number) into BOTH files. That is what puts "esr"
#   into MOZ_APP_VERSION, and it has a second consequence beyond this build
#   failure: init.configure:1151 computes
#         is_esr = app_version_display.endswith("esr") or None
#   and "153.0esr-1" does not end with "esr", so **MOZ_ESR is not set on the
#   LibreWolf Android/ESR tree** - verified, it is absent from config.status.
#   That flips two `#ifndef MOZ_ESR` blocks on: ".jnlp" is included in
#   xpcom/io/nsLocalFileCommon.cpp's sExecutableExts (113 entries, not 112) and
#   in the ApplicationReputation list. Both are the *stricter* branch, so this is
#   not a security regression - but it is an unintended difference between what
#   the tree says it is and what it is, and it belongs in the M5 parity matrix.
#
#   The clean fix for both is in scripts/librewolf-patches.py / ./version.android
#   - stop conflating the release-track name with Firefox's version number - and
#   LW-M2-02 does not own either file. Flagged rather than done. This hunk stays
#   correct either way: with a fixed version.txt the `esr$` strip is a no-op.
#
# THE FIX: teach getAppVersionWithoutMilestone() about the two suffixes
# LibreWolf's version string can carry, so that only the dotted numeric version
# is ever parsed. `getVersionNumber()` (build.gradle:223-233) and the equivalent
# helper in mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/engine-gecko/
# build.gradle:113-128 also call a getAppVersionWithoutMilestone(), but neither
# parses integers - they only take parts[0] and parts[1] - so neither was
# failing, and the android-components copy is deliberately left alone.
#
# WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO, and the two alternatives that were rejected
#
#   a) Stop appending "-<release>" to version.txt on Android. That would make
#      MOZ_APP_VERSION on Android a bare Firefox version, so about:buildconfig
#      and GeckoView's BuildConfig.MOZ_APP_VERSION (mobile/android/geckoview/
#      build.gradle) would no longer name the LibreWolf release at all, and
#      Android would report a different version from desktop for the same
#      source. It also means adding a *second* target-dependent out-of-patch
#      mutation to scripts/librewolf-patches.py, which is the failure class
#      landmine L4 warns about, in a file this task does not own.
#
#   b) Create mobile/android/config/version{,_display}.txt so init.configure
#      picks those up instead. Same loss of the LibreWolf version on Android,
#      plus a second copy of the version number to keep in sync, plus a third
#      out-of-patch mutation.
#
#   Doing it here keeps the LibreWolf version string intact everywhere it is
#   user-visible, and keeps the change inside the patch set where
#   `make check-patchfail` can see it drift.
#
# KNOWN LIMITATION - hand this to LW-M2-04 / LW-M6 (store distribution)
#
#   versionCode is now computed from the Firefox version alone: 153.0.4-1 and a
#   hypothetical 153.0.4-2 both yield 15300004, and on the ESR track 153.0esr-1
#   yields 15300000. A LibreWolf-only release bump therefore does NOT advance
#   versionCode, and both Google Play and F-Droid require it to increase for
#   every published artifact. Upstream's scheme (major*100000 + minor*100 +
#   build, "must be synchronized with _compute_gecko_version(...) in
#   taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/task.py") leaves no free digits, so
#   folding the release number in is a versioning-scheme decision, not a build
#   fix, and it is deliberately not made here. It does not affect the GeckoView
#   AAR that `mach build` produces today.
#
# REBASE CHECK: if upstream rewrites getAppVersionWithoutMilestone(), this hunk
# rejects. Do not paper over it - re-read computeVersionCode() and check what it
# does with a version string carrying a "-N" suffix before regenerating.
#
--- a/build.gradle
+++ b/build.gradle
@@ -168,8 +168,23 @@
 // Non-official versions are like "61.0a1" or "61.0b1", where "a1" and "b1"
 // are the milestone.
 // This simply strips that off, leaving "61.0" in this example.
+//
+// LibreWolf: MOZ_APP_VERSION is not a bare Firefox version here.
+// scripts/librewolf-patches.py rewrites browser/config/version{,_display}.txt
+// to "<firefox version>-<librewolf release>", and the Android track pins an
+// ESR version, so the value reaching this function is "153.0.4-1" on the
+// release track and "153.0esr-1" on the ESR track. Upstream only strips an
+// [ab][0-9] milestone, so computeVersionCode() below fed Integer.parseInt()
+// "4-1" (release track) or "0esr-1" (ESR track) and threw
+// NumberFormatException while Gradle was still evaluating the root project --
+// i.e. before a single line of Gecko was compiled. Strip the LibreWolf
+// release suffix and the "esr" tag as well, so what is parsed is always the
+// dotted numeric version.
 def getAppVersionWithoutMilestone() {
-    return project.ext.mozconfig.substs.MOZ_APP_VERSION.replaceFirst(/[ab][0-9]/, "")
+    return project.ext.mozconfig.substs.MOZ_APP_VERSION
+            .replaceFirst(/-.*$/, "")
+            .replaceFirst(/esr$/, "")
+            .replaceFirst(/[ab][0-9]/, "")
 }

 // This converts MOZ_APP_VERSION into an integer
